From a166384933e6041995b4127991b8f9fd0454d0b5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 09:24:38 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] docs + protected-wins: the R18 switch table - eight
 DOCUMENTED-TAKE runtime switches registered with their measured effect

docs/OPTIONS-REGISTRY.md: one row per switch (GGML_ARIFI_FA_DEQUANT_KV, LLAMA_DFLASH_FUSED_INJECT, GGML_ARIFI_MMV_ID_ROWS, LLAMA_KV_NGRAM_INDEX, the MUL_MAT_ID staging receipt + tq_rotate assert, GGML_ARIFI_UMA_READ_PATH, GGML_TYPE_SX8, and the TBQ3_0/TBQ4_0 pair with LLAMA_ALLOW_TBQ3_KV), each carrying its default, its scope, when to touch it and its measured cost. A blockquote above the discipline section states what DOCUMENTED-TAKE means and quotes the build floor the numbers must be read against, so no row can be mistaken for a performance recommendation.

tools/arifi-sync/protected-wins.json: seven new active entries, one per merged candidate, with protected_paths, source-only anchors, symbol definitions where a definition can be lost while its declaration survives (WI-1700 class), evidence paths, quality_gate and workload. status is 'active' - the schema enumerates active|superseded only, so the DOCUMENTED-TAKE verdict is carried in measured_effect, where it belongs. protected-win validate PASSes 30 entries / 52 paths / 72 anchors / 45 symbols.

AMENDED, because the register was carrying a claim the wave falsified: vulkan-fa-dequant-kv-runtime-gate's measured_effect now records that R19D's +8.08% prefill DOES NOT REPRODUCE on recomputation from the banked rounds (gate OFF vs ON on one binary: decode +0.49% CI95 [-1.62%, +2.59%], prefill +0.85% [+0.36%, +1.33%]). The knob, the receipt and the ON default stand; the magnitude does not, and the registry row says so too.

No default is claimed as a win anywhere in this table. Two rows record a deliberate divergence from upstream and say why in the row itself: LLAMA_DFLASH_FUSED_INJECT defaults to legacy on a sub-floor number, and LLAMA_KV_NGRAM_INDEX keeps the upstream indexed default against the R38 brief's instruction.

Origin: ArifiLabs lane-225 R38 merge of the R18 kernel wave DOCUMENTED-TAKEs (Opus 5 MEDIUM, kernel-maker)
Measured-effect: none - registry and manifest only, no code path touched
Lane: lane-225
